WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:10.520
When y'all were living in the evacuation center at the Municipal Auditorium, what were the issues that were happening there?

2
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.960
The issues of concern?

3
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.620
Well, it was . . . For one thing, it was overcrowded.

4
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.660
The people weren't as friendly, you know.

5
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:26.060
I was really glad to get out because I had all the kids with me.

6
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.720
And I didn't want them to be in the building over the night.

7
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.640
They were overcrowded.

8
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.240
They had people walking on one another.

9
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.740
You're trying to sleep, and everybody's walking all around you.

10
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.020
No bunks.

11
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.320
I could remember nobody slept that night.

12
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.200
We stayed in one little corner, you know.

13
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.100
Like wherever we was, but we was in one little corner.

14
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:57.360
"Francis [?], look at the water coming up to the first step."

15
00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.840
I said, "If that water get up a little higher we're going to have to get out."

16
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.880
"Oh no." He says, "It ain't going to get up no higher than the steps!"

17
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:07.160
He thought it wasn't, you know.

18
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.720
And so, girl!

19
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.820
That water came in this house, you wouldn't believe it!

20
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.040
Just like a ship had then passed.

21
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.900
Big furniture was turned upside down.

22
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.500
Everything was tumbled up and down in this house.

23
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.860
I was worried about the kids.

24
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:28.540
Man, I was worried about getting them out of here.

25
00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.380
So that's when I put all the kids in the attic.

26
00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.820
And I say, "Francis, that water's up to the step."

27
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:40.400
"Oh," he says, "I don't think it's going to get any higher." [laughs] And the water got so high!

28
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.160
And that's how we got caught in this house.

29
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:47.300
Because if he had left when I first told him, we wouldn't have got in it either.

30
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:52.640
A lot of people, like I said, they must have left when the water first was coming.

31
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.900
See, because when that water was coming, it was coming in kind of slower.

32
00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.620
Then later on, that water was coming rough.

33
00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.260
Just like a dike just busted open.

34
00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:07.180
And that water started coming in here, boy, it wasn't funny.

35
00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.660
And that was something.

36
00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.760
Never want to live that through again?

37
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:12.960
Yeah.

38
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.840
No, indeed.

39
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.280
That water was something.
